---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContactCta from '../../../components/ContactCta.astro';

const locale = 'en' as const;
---

<Layout
  locale={locale}
  title="IT Governance & OSFI Compliance | Monessor"
  description="IT governance review, third-party risk management, and regulatory alignment (OSFI B-10, B-13, E-23) for growing financial institutions and FinTechs."
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="kicker">IT Governance, Risk &amp; Compliance • Financial Services &amp; FinTech</p>
      <h1>Navigate regulatory rigor without paralyzing your platforms' pace of innovation.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Monessor designs and validates IT governance frameworks, third-party risk management, and regulatory
        alignment (OSFI - B-10, B-13, E-23) for growing financial institutions and FinTechs.
      </p>

      <div class="microproof">
        <div class="pill">OSFI Alignment</div>
        <div class="pill">Compliance by Design</div>
        <div class="pill">Institutional Expertise</div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-cta">
        <ContactCta
          href="https://calendar.app.google/jrWp3LMihMCr5qew7"
          label="Schedule a meeting"
          ariaLabel="Schedule a meeting"
          className="btn"
          fathomEventName="Click ScheduleMeeting Service-RegFS-Hero"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- REGULATORY COMPLIANCE CHALLENGES -->
  <section class="section" id="issues">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Where traditional governance paralyzes execution</h2>

      <div class="cards mt-6">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Mounting OSFI requirements</h3>
          <p>
            Growing complexity in complying with cyber risk management guidelines (B-13), operational resilience,
            and third-party risk (B-10).
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>The illusion of “paper” compliance</h3>
          <p>
            Policies written for auditors but disconnected from the reality of the code deployed to production by
            engineering teams and Cloud vendors.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>AI &amp; Complex Model Risk (E-23)</h3>
          <p>
            The challenge of governing the integration of algorithms and automated decision-making models without
            slowing down digital product development.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Friction between Risk and Delivery</h3>
          <p>
            Heavy validation committees that slow down go-to-market cycles and create tension between the
            Risk/Compliance function and Product teams.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ENTRY OFFER: IT GOVERNANCE & OSFI COMPLIANCE REVIEW -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="review">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="kicker">01 / REGULATORY AUDIT &amp; ALIGNMENT</p>
      <h2>IT Governance &amp; OSFI Compliance Review</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        A 3- to 4-week executive mandate to audit technology compliance, identify third-party risk gaps, and
        deliver a remediation matrix the Risk and Audit Committee can act on directly.
      </p>
      <p class="lead" style="font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent);">
        Starting at $18,500 CAD <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400; color: var(--muted);">(Fixed-scope engagement)</span>
      </p>

      <div class="bullets">
        <div class="bullet">
          <p class="bullet-title">OSFI B-10 / B-13 Gap Analysis</p>
          <p>
            Concrete alignment audit of your infrastructure and policies against Canadian regulatory requirements.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bullet">
          <p class="bullet-title">Third-Party Risk Audit</p>
          <p>
            Assessment of critical technology dependencies, vendor contract analysis, and validation of business
            continuity plans (BCPs).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bullet">
          <p class="bullet-title">AI &amp; Data Governance Framework (E-23 Alignment)</p>
          <p>
            Definition of architectural guardrails and explainability mechanisms for the use of AI in a regulated
            context.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bullet">
          <p class="bullet-title">Remediation Matrix &amp; Executive Action Plan</p>
          <p>
            Risk-prioritized roadmap to satisfy auditor and regulator requirements.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-cta">
        <ContactCta
          href="https://calendar.app.google/jrWp3LMihMCr5qew7"
          label="Schedule a meeting"
          ariaLabel="Schedule a meeting"
          className="btn"
          fathomEventName="Click ScheduleMeeting Service-RegFS-Review"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- EXECUTIVE PRACTICE AREAS -->
  <section class="section" id="approach">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Deep expertise for high-risk environments</h2>

      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <p class="step-num">01</p>
          <h3>Compliance by Design</h3>
          <p>
            Automated integration of regulatory constraints (OSFI) directly into deployment pipelines (CI/CD) and
            Cloud architectures, without slowing down developers.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <p class="step-num">02</p>
          <h3>Support During Regulatory Audits</h3>
          <p>
            Consultative presence alongside leadership during internal audit reviews, external audits, or
            examinations by financial market authorities.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <p class="step-num">03</p>
          <h3>Model Governance &amp; Responsible AI</h3>
          <p>
            Oversight of predictive and generative model lifecycles to ensure auditability and security.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CROSS-LINK -->
  <section class="section" id="established-smbs">
    <div class="container" style="text-align: center;">
      <div class="card" style="max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
          Leading an industrial or distribution SMB?
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn--outline" href="/en/services/fractional-cto-smb/">Discover our IT Diagnostic &amp; AI Alignment offer →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- EXECUTIVE PRACTICE POSITIONING -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="positioning">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="kicker">Executive Practice Positioning</p>
      <h2>Engineering rigor, not just a legal opinion.</h2>

      <div class="note">
        <p>
          « Monessor is not a law firm or a traditional accounting audit firm. We combine a deep understanding of
          OSFI requirements with software architecture expertise to make your systems genuinely compliant in
          practice, not only on paper. »
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
